Net effect: ball pushed to brick.y - r (above lower brick = in the gap region above it), vy flipped twice → negative again. Still plows through.

So processing multiple bricks in one pass with push-out and flip still cancels. The issue says "the bounce must apply exactly once". So we need to ensure only ONE brick gets the bounce per pass — e.g., break after the first resolved collision, or mark the ball as "already bounced" this pass.

